// Strict typecheck gate for test files (WAVE_A_ON_MAIN.md open issue 2; QA F140, F188, F225).
// Run: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.test.json (CI: the "Typecheck changed tests" step of the test job).
// tsconfig.json excludes every *.test.ts(x), so `tsc -p tsconfig.json` says nothing about tests.
//
// In scope: next-env.d.ts, every test file added or modified since main 7224f40 as of 718752e
// (140 files, from `git diff --name-only --diff-filter=AM 7224f40 HEAD | grep -E '(\.test\.tsx?$|__tests__/.*\.tsx?$)'`),
// and any file named src/**/hardening-*.test.ts or src/**/hardening-*.test.tsx. Files those import are checked too.
// The list is explicit, so the gate needs no git base in CI. A new test file either follows the hardening-* naming
// or is added to this list.
//
// Out of scope: main's pre-existing errors in untouched tests. Measured by H9 with every test file under src
// included (src/**/*.test.ts(x) and src/**/__tests__/**/*.ts(x), same compiler options): 755 errors in 151 files at
// 718752e; after H9, 671 errors in 130 files outside this list, by directory:
//   src/app/api 210 errors (10 files), src/lib/adaptive 154 (36), src/lib/studio 109 (27), src/app/studio 69 (24),
//   src/lib/connections 52 (15), src/stores 35 (5), src/lib/tireh 34 (9), src/lib/legacy-inventory 4 (1),
//   src/lib/relationships 2 (2), src/lib/guest-privacy-sentry.test.ts 2 (1).
// 54 of them are process.env literals that become errors only because a test in that wider program imports a Next page or
// layout, which loads Next's global types (NODE_ENV required). The task brief quoted 346 errors in about 104 files;
// the counts above are H9's own measurement on this tree.
//
// Known limits:
// - circles-group.test.ts and adaptive/personalization/learning/races.test.ts have test-only fixes from H9 but are
//   not listed: they carry 12 and 2 of main's pre-existing errors (zero-argument mock tuples, a read-only assignment).
// - next-env.d.ts is generated by `next dev` / `next build` and is absent in CI's test job. Where it exists (a local
//   checkout after a dev run), Next's global types make NODE_ENV a required ProcessEnv key, and env literals typed as
//   NodeJS.ProcessEnv in five listed files (tireh flags, memory-v2-retrieval, qa-spec-conformance-r3; studio
//   voiceprint-storage, decisions-runtime) report 43 more errors. The same happens if a listed test imports a Next
//   page or layout. CI is not affected; fixing those files belongs to their owners.
